    modified_response: "I have completed the Linux Voice Assistant, bridging real-time AI audio processing with actual system execution capabilities.\n\n-   **Cybernetic Command Interface**: Designed a sleek, hacker-inspired dark theme emphasizing high contrast and technical precision. The UI features real-time pulse animations and a reactive microphone module.\n-   **Low-Latency Intercom Tunnel**: Configured a WebSocket linkage routing raw 16kHz PCM audio buffers between the browser and the Express backend, bridging directly to the Gemini Live API for sub-second conversational latency.\n-   **System-Wide Execution Engine**: Implemented an overarching `runLinuxCommand` function callback on the server side. As you speak to the assistant, it dynamically determines when to interpret your words as bash commands (`ls`, `uptime`, system stats) and executes them directly on the hosting instance.\n\n*Note: While running in this isolated cloud preview environment, system commands are restricted to the sandboxed Linux container boundaries. When you download and run this application natively (`npm run start`) on your local machine, the assistant will assume the system permissions of your host.*"
