  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Presentation Design**\n\nI\'ve been working on refining the presentation. I\'m focusing on making purely CSS and structural layout adjustments to the containers. So far, I\'ve adjusted the parent container wrappers and made some introductions to improve the overall design.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have successfully applied the \"Frosted Glass\" design theme to the Nexus OS Assistant based on the provided design specifications.\n\n**Theme Implementation Highlights:**\n- **Frosted Containers:** Converted the interface entirely to use highly polished, frosted translucent panels featuring strong backdrop blurring (`backdrop-blur-2xl`) with subtle semi-transparent `white/5` and `white/10` borders to give the illusion of layers of glass.\n- **Ambient Lighting:** Introduced the mesh gradient background overlays utilizing `indigo-600/20` and `emerald-500/10` light blobs that sit gently beneath the user interface layer.\n- **The Central \"Orb\" & Pulse rings:** Redesigned the main listening visualizer to use the requested smooth gradient ring (`bg-gradient-to-tr from-indigo-600 to-emerald-400`); the mic functionality integrates tightly with the interactive animations provided by the theme. \n- **Refined Event List (`Event Horizon`):** Reskinned the logging panel with a clean structural grid layout pattern (`grid-cols-12`) placing the event horizon dynamically into the UI alongside a redesigned Live status transcript bar on the bottom.\n\nAll functionalities including the host WebSocket interactions, logging components, and animation states have been perfectly preserved and merged into the new aesthetic."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 885217356
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
