  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Autonomy in AI**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining \"fully autonomous\" for the AI assistant. The core concept is listening for a wake word, connecting, completing the task, and potentially disconnecting, but also being able to remain listening. This should enable completely hands-free use. The user\342\200\231s input about \"no need to press a button\" is now the primary focus.\n\n\n**Refining Autonomous Operation**\n\nI\'ve been working on integrating `toggleWakeWord` using SpeechRecognition and aiming for an always-listening state. The goal is seamless, hands-free operation. I\'m exploring automatic wake word listening on app start and considering the best way to handle the Gemini Live session, potentially keeping it open or using its VAD. The UI is also being considered for modern looks.\n\n\n**Addressing Audio Streaming Concerns**\n\nI\'m now grappling with the implications of always-listening modes. Auto-connecting presents issues with constant audio streaming and associated costs and privacy concerns. I\'m exploring a local wake word detection strategy using the Web Speech API to initiate Gemini Live, but I\'m concerned about the high streaming costs associated with Gemini Live. I\'m now implementing automatic wake word listening on app load. I\'ll need to figure out what to do with the Gemini Live session, keeping it active all the time.\n\n\n**Addressing Browser Permissions**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag: browsers block automatic `SpeechRecognition`. I need to add a user gesture, like a \"Initiate System\" button on an overlay. Once clicked, it initializes the `AudioContext` and wake word listener. The goal is to provide a clean, modern UI, using frosted glass, glassy animations, and better typography. My next step involves the `App.tsx` overlay implementation.\n\n\n**Implementing Session Disconnect**\n\nI\'m now integrating a \"disconnectSession\" tool to explicitly end conversations. The plan involves the AI using this tool when the user says \"goodbye\". The server will then send a specific message to the client via WebSockets to initiate the disconnection. I\'m refactoring `server.ts` to accommodate this new tool and the WebSocket communication needed for proper session termination.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 750936211
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
